__pycache__/
temp/
backend/certs/
# Wrangler's local build state, written by ``wrangler dev`` / ``wrangler deploy`` from
# deploy/cloudflare/. Machine-specific and regenerated on every run, like a venv.
.wrangler/
# ONNX liveness model: a binary artifact that does not belong in git history.
# Place it at backend/models/minifasnet.onnx (see backend/models/README.md).
backend/models/*.onnx
backend/models/*.onnx.*
# ...except the face detector and the embedding engine. The YuNet detector (232 KB) is
# the difference between a 10 ms and a 308 ms detection on every punch, and
# facenet128.onnx (87 MB) is the embedding engine itself - the startup gate REFUSES to
# serve without a band's model present, so either one missing from a Railway build is an
# app that never boots. Both ship with the code instead of behind a deploy step.
!backend/models/face_detection_yunet_2023mar.onnx
!backend/models/facenet128.onnx
times.db
# SQLite sidecar files created by WAL mode while the server runs
times.db-wal
times.db-shm
.env
# The Railway service variables an operator applies by hand (VAPID key pair, trusted proxies).
# Same class as .env above: VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY signs pushes as this deployment to every endpoint
# it has stored, so it is a secret, and the file exists so it never has to be pasted into an
# issue, a log or a screenshot. 
# deploy/railway/README.md documents every value in it.
deploy/railway/variables.env
worker_photos
local_references
# Selfies taken with a quick clock link. Biometric data, like the two above: never in git.
quick_link_photos
# The frame stored with each punch, for a review card. Same class again: a worker's face, and
# the app writes one of these per punch. It was the only one of the four left unignored, so a
# test run that stored a frame left the checkout with hundreds of untracked JPEGs.
punch_frames
.vscode
# The Dockerfile is the deployment artifact Railway builds from (railway.json names it);
# ignoring the file that deploys the service is how the image and the repo drift apart.
!Dockerfile
!.dockerignore
test_odoo.py
backups/

# The virtualenv is rebuilt per machine (see backend/requirements-optional.txt and the
# note at the top of requirements-dev.txt); its 26k files are not the project.
backend/venv/
# Freebuff's own worktrees live here, and a git worktree inside a worktree is not a
# thing to commit.
.freebuff/